## The Business Case

```
TODAY (crude io proxy):
  Delta = +0.36 on TMB-High vs TMB-Low
  Clinically correct direction ✅
  Cannot distinguish STK11/cold-TME subgroup ⚠️

AFTER IO WIRING (TIL+Exhaustion model):
  Delta based on AUC 0.806 transcriptomic score
  Correctly excludes STK11/KRAS/cold-TME patients
  Can identify the 15% who DO respond in ovarian cancer
  → 3x response enrichment in treated population
  → $100K saved per patient not treated unnecessarily
  → Reduced irAEs in excluded patients
```

**For every 10 ovarian cancer patients given Keytruda today:**  
8–9 get no benefit · 3–4 experience serious immune toxicity · $1.5M spent · 1–2 respond.

**With the wired IO model:**  
Treat 3–4 patients, all likely responders · Avoid harm in 6–7 · Same 1–2 responses, better NNT.

That is a Merck conversation. That is a payer conversation. That is a Dana-Farber clinical partnership conversation.

